.TH SDL_GetRenderOutputSize 3 "SDL 3.5.0" "Simple Directmedia Layer" "SDL3 FUNCTIONS"
.SH NAME
SDL_GetRenderOutputSize \- Get the output size in pixels of a rendering context.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <SDL3/SDL_render.h>
.PP
.BI "bool SDL_GetRenderOutputSize(SDL_Renderer *renderer, int *w, int *h);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
This returns the true output size in pixels, ignoring any render targets or logical size and presentation\[char46]
.PP
For the output size of the current rendering target, with logical size adjustments, use
.BR SDL_GetCurrentRenderOutputSize ()
instead\[char46]

.SH FUNCTION PARAMETERS
.TP
.I renderer
the rendering context\[char46]
.TP
.I w
a pointer filled in with the width in pixels\[char46]
.TP
.I h
a pointer filled in with the height in pixels\[char46]
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns true on success or false on failure; call
.BR SDL_GetError ()
for more information\[char46]

.SH THREAD SAFETY
This function should only be called on the main thread\[char46]

.SH AVAILABILITY
This function is available since SDL 3\[char46]2\[char46]0\[char46]

.SH SEE ALSO
.BR SDL_GetCurrentRenderOutputSize (3)
